  "title": "design-map-stage-fills-the-panel-body",
  "requirement": "AC-1 / FR1 / REQ-251: in Design map mode the stage fills the panel body (no 620px cap, no page scroll) and grows with the window; at 1440x900 the stage is at least 500px tall. This case checks the panel CSS contract that produces that layout; the 1440x900 pixel height is the implementer's browser proof (reports/designmap-instruments/proof.out), not re-measured here.",
  "kind": "regression",
  "status": "verified",
  "source": "agent",
  "automated": true,
  "testPath": "tests/designmap-instruments/panel-surface.mjs",
  "runCommand": "node tests/designmap-instruments/panel-surface.mjs --case AC-1",
  "steps": [
    "Read the panel client source of the tree under test (current tree, or the pre-fix worktree when cwd is that copy).",
    "Extract the .ps-main-map, .ps-mapstage and .ps-main-map .ps-mapstage rules and the map-mode branch.",
    "Assert padding 0, overflow hidden, flex column, height 100%, flex 1, border 0, no min(64vh) anywhere, and the editor mounted in the stage."
  ],
  "expected": "The map body rule (.ps-main-map) drops the reading padding and page scroll and is a flex column; the stage rule (.ps-mapstage) has height 100%, no min(64vh)/620px cap and no border; .ps-main-map .ps-mapstage is the flex child; the map section carries ps-main-map only in map mode and mounts the page editor inside the stage.",
